% Probe: can a PDF named destination be registered from an `inline-graphics`
% callback?
%
% Run BOTH engines --- here they DISAGREE, which is the point:
%
%   layout-tests/tools/probe.py layout-tests/probes/inline_graphics_dest.saty
%
%   SATySFi 0.0.11   renders, and the anchor lands in the PDF
%   this port        Error: register-destination can only be called during
%                    page breaking (from a page-break hook or a decoration)
%
% Upstream and this port agree on the GATE --- `annotation.ml:15` raises
% `State.NotDuringPageBreak` outside the window too, so relaxing it here would
% be the unfaithful fix. They disagree on WHEN the callback runs.
% `primitives.rs`'s `prim_inline_graphics` documents the deviation as its
% "eager-callback shortcut": a lang closure cannot live inside a
% `PureHorzBox::Graphics`, so the callback is applied once at construction
% time at `(0pt, 0pt)` (and a second time at a probe point, to detect a
% page-absolute callback) and the writer's per-box `cm` supplies the placed
% position later. That is exact for a shift-covariant graphics generator and
% wrong for a SIDE-EFFECTING one: at construction time no page exists, so
% `interp.current_page` is `None`.
%
% Measured on azmath (satysfi-azmath 0.0.3), whose `equation.satyh`
% `ib-annotation` is exactly the shape below --- it anchors every `\label`ed
% equation. With this one call stubbed out the port builds azmath's whole
% 30-page-source manual (14 pages, 619 lines against upstream's 15), so this
% single primitive-timing gap is all that keeps azmath out of `corpus/`.
% Closing it needs the deferred-firing architecture the `deco` family already
% has: the destination's key would ride in the `Graphics` box and be resolved
% to `(page, x, y)` by `fire_hooks`, which already walks that box.
@require: stdjabook

let-inline ctx \anchor key =
  inline-graphics 0pt 0pt 0pt (fun (x, y) -> (
    let () = register-destination key (x, y) in []
  ))
in

document (|
  title = {inline-graphics destination probe};
  author = {};
  show-title = false;
  show-toc = false;
|) '<
  +p{before \anchor(`probe-dest`); after}
>
